                            # re-open on THAT number, never on this one.

mrnet_warm_s2026.pt         # DECLINED as a seat, checkpoint kept. 0.8487 peak e6, CONVERGED (12 of 12; the one_cycle anneal loses 0.004 rather than
  gaining, so e6 is the recipe's ceiling and not a floor). THE PROJECT'S FIRST EXTERNAL-CORPUS MEMBER:
  trunk warm-started from mrnet_acl_pretrain_s2026 (its epoch 7, 225 tensors, 11 head tensors left cold),
  pretrained on MRNet knee MRI. Rule 2.6 permits it; the CC/RUA copyright question is knee-ib4t and is
  about redistribution, not about training here. It was ROSTERED on 2026-09-03 as a hypothesis about
  diversity, with the line saying in writing that the seat was settled by a vote_ceiling reading and not
  by that line. This is that reading, and it declines it.

  THE SEAT IS WORTH ZERO, measured three ways on the twinfive_v1 pool - the fold-0 five, the only
  scoreable roster this project still has, since the champion's six are all --fold -1 and unscoreable by
  construction. Both arms use the SAME pool, so the delta is legitimate; only an absolute number would
  cross the --fold -1 line.
    vote_ceiling, LogitAverage, honest split-half:  5 members 0.8706 -> 6 members 0.8705  (-0.0001)
    seat_value --against twinfive_v1, added sixth:  -0.0000, band [-0.0010, +0.0009]
    seat_value, best SWAP (for lr4e-5_ws_s2026):    +0.0004, against BOARD_RESOLVABLE 0.0040

  AND THE DECORRELATION IS REAL, WHICH IS WHY THIS IS A DECLINE AND NOT A NULL. MemberDistance puts its
  nearest neighbour at 0.8892, inside the roster's own nearest spread (0.8696 to 0.8972), so it is not a
  twin; its MEAN correlation of 0.8552 is lower than any seated member's NEAREST, making it the most
  globally distant candidate this pool has been offered. It still buys 0.0000. So knee-nj4l's monoculture
  claim is NOT refuted here - it is untested by this member. Corpus distance on the SAME lens (a DINOv2
  trunk warm-started elsewhere) produces measurable ordering distance and zero seat value. What remains
  unmeasured is ARCHITECTURE distance, which is what ortho_pool_read is on the card for.

  THE SPECIALIST RESCUE WAS TRIED AND FAILED. MRNet's pretraining task is ACL tear, and mrnet leads the
  whole pool on ACL solo: 0.8840 against depth_regions_narrow 0.8737, calib_span 0.8706, lr4e-5_ws 0.8706
  - plus 0.0103 on the one label its corpus was built for, which is exactly the shape a specialist has.
  Its 0.8487 mean is dragged down elsewhere (Fracture 0.7954 against 0.8253, PF OA 0.8192), and a
  per-label rank average charges that weakness eleven times against one strength. So the obvious rescue
  is to seat it on ACL only. Measured, per label, LogitAverage over the same five vs the same six:
    ACL +0.0014   MCL +0.0027   MedMen +0.0008   LatMen +0.0003   MedOA -0.0008   LatOA +0.0017
    PFOA -0.0027  Effusion +0.0006  Synovitis -0.0014  Baker's -0.0021  Contusion +0.0020  Fracture -0.0019
  Seven up, five down, largest move 0.0027, mean +0.0000. The ACL specialism does not survive into the
  pool because the pool is ALREADY at 0.9011 on ACL - well above mrnet's 0.8840 solo. A member cannot
  lift a label it is worse at than the vote already is.

  RE-OPEN BY, and not by re-quoting 0.8487: (a) an external-corpus member whose TRUNK differs, not whose
  corpus does - the axis this one holds fixed; (b) a per-label reading on a label where the POOL is weak
  and the external corpus is strong, which ACL is not (MCL 0.8114 and Lateral OA 0.8249 are the pool's
  two weakest, and MRNet supervises neither). The checkpoint is kept; only the seat is refused.

ortho_pool_read.pt  # A PROBE, and it was never a seat candidate. It exists to read one thing: whether
  `ortholarge` - DINOv3-L weights moved by 1.25M knee-MRI slices - carries knee structure a natural-image
  trunk does not. Peak 0.8464 at epoch 8, below both the 0.8492 floor edge and the 0.8521 non-DINOv2 seat
  bar, so it is DIRECTIONAL and nothing more; the reading it was armed for is the LP-FT triple, which is
  still one control short (knee-6hfi, `ortho_fresh_lowlr`).

  IT IS ALSO NOT SHIPPABLE TODAY, for a reason that has nothing to do with the number. `ortholarge`'s
  release licence is unresolved against the fastMRI DSA the continuation corpus may draw on - knee-nxthh,
  and Kimi's Q-CE is outstanding on exactly this. Rostering it would declare shippable a member whose
  right to ship is an open question, which is the failure mode `mount_check` catches one step too late.

  RE-OPEN BY: Q-CE resolving PERMIT, plus a score that clears 0.8521. Either alone is not enough - the
  licence gates the seat and the number gates the merit, and this member currently fails both.

