#
# --- The DINOv3 decode family: VOID. The coat384 mirage at twice the size. ---------------------------
# These read the best numbers in the project - solo up to 0.8959 tying our ceiling, nn-corr 0.734 against
# a pool median of 0.9161, swaps +0.0060/+0.0117/+0.0100, and they COMPOUND on top of repl2x2_c. None of
# it is real. experiments/arms/foreign_decode_fine.sh is a BAND SWEEP OVER A SERVED PROGRAM, not a
# training run - :34 says --band is the only moving variable and their lifted program is otherwise
# untouched, :7 calls 0.12-0.88 the band their released kernel serves - and it serves mattiaangeli's
# released fold weights m_f0.pt..m_f4.pt unchanged. So all of them inherit the defect that voided the
# sibling dinov3f0_solo at members.declines:698-703: IN-SAMPLE ON 703 OF 909 by the md5 split, fold 0
# holding only 206. Our 896-row frame is OUR fold-0 holdout, not theirs.
#
# The signature is worth keeping because it fired twice in one night: solo inflated to our ceiling,
# correlation COLLAPSED (no honest member of ours can reproduce memorised rows), and seat value scaling
# with the contamination rather than with skill. coat384 was +0.0039/+0.0065/+0.0053 against honest
# +0.0019-0.0031; these are +0.0060/+0.0117/+0.0100. The magnitude of a mirage is proportional to the
# contamination and bounded by nothing, so "this number is too good" is a real prior.
#
# THE DISCRIMINATOR THAT WORKS (D148 section 3): not the npz fields, not the row count - our honest
# calib_span_s2026 carries the identical 909-row set - but WHETHER A LOCAL ARM TRAINED THE WEIGHTS.
# repl2x2 has after_cellc.sh plus a [cv] fold 0/1 log line; these have a decode arm that says in its own
# comments that it serves someone else's program.
#
# RE-OPENED ONLY BY AN OUR-FOLD REFIT OF THE RECIPE, NEVER BY RE-QUOTING THESE NUMBERS.
