latent_register_deep_s2026.pt        # 0.8378 solo — below the 0.8459 merit level this pool has ever added at, AND Pearson 0.9427 against latent_register_dense_s2026 (rostered) across all 10908 holdout cells. Same trunk, same recipe, one flag apart (mask 0.60 vs 0.30), and the two fine-tunes track within +/-0.002 for nine consecutive epochs. dense is rostered for DIVERSITY, being the only v3small trunk carrying an on-domain latent-MIM adaptation; a second near-copy of it does not extend that argument. Re-open by naming what it would be an instrument FOR — not by re-quoting the solo.
v3small_control_s2026.pt             # 0.8371 solo — the unadapted zero point for the latent-MIM family, and it did its job: it priced `latent_register_dense` at +0.0014 and `latent_register_deep` at +0.0007, which closed the adaptation axis (ledger 2026-09-09). Declined as a SEAT, not as a member: it is a plain published v3small at the pool's lowest merit level, and the pool already carries v3small trunks that beat it on solo AND carry something it does not. Its value is as a CONTROL and it keeps that value on disk. Re-open by naming an ensemble reading where an unadapted v3small adds where the adapted one does not — that would make it a diversity seat, which is the only argument it could win on.
